{# Java {Bidder}Bidder.java template — emits
src/main/java/org/prebid/server/bidder/{bidder}/{Bidder}Bidder.java

This is the heaviest template in the port-go2java suite. The template
covers the canonical shapes observed across the MVP corpus (kobler,
aax, adkernelAdn, adverxo, vungle, thetradedesk) plus a few common
variants. Source-spec shapes outside this set surface as
unresolved_translations[] in the port-report (the SKILL Step 3 falls
through to a TODO comment in the emitted Java; the operator hand-fills
post-emit).

Inputs (large; see the prose-driven SKILL Step 4 docstring for what
the SKILL passes from the source spec):

  ctx.bidder_name              : str  — Java YAML / package name (lowercase)
  ctx.bidder_class_root        : str  — PascalCase (e.g., "Kobler", "AdkernelAdn")
  ctx.uses_currency_conversion : bool — source spec's currency_conversion.used
  ctx.imp_ext_class_root       : str  — typically same as bidder_class_root; used for ExtImp{X}
  ctx.imp_ext_unmarshal_kind   : str  — one of {"standard-two-phase", "direct"}; Rule 1/2
  ctx.batching_kind            : str  — one of {"single-batched", "per-imp", "max-imps-per-request",
                                          "grouped-by-key", "format-split", "pod-grouping"};
                                          Rule 16/17/18/47. NOTE the cross-skill spelling
                                          asymmetry: this value tracks the SPEC driver
                                          (`batching.rules[].kind: grouped-by-key`), while
                                          port-java2go's ctx spells the same kind "per-key".
                                          Both feed a ctx.batching_per_key dict.
  ctx.batching_max_imps        : int|null  — when batching_kind == "max-imps-per-request"
  ctx.batching_per_key         : dict|null — Rule 47, when batching_kind ==
                                          "grouped-by-key". Selects WHAT the groups are keyed
                                          on. Two shapes, both drawn from merged upstream
                                          adapters:
                                            absent / key_field null
                                              Key on the WHOLE ExtImp{X} object:
                                              `Map<ExtImp{X}, List<Imp>>`. This is the default
                                              because it is what upstream does most —
                                              AdkernelBidder, DatablocksBidder and
                                              ZeroclickfraudBidder all key on their ext type,
                                              and every Go grouper does the same
                                              (`map[openrtb_ext.ExtImp{X}][]openrtb2.Imp`), so
                                              it is also what port-java2go emits. Requires the
                                              ext POJO to carry `@Value` for equals/hashCode,
                                              which ext-imp-pojo.java.j2 emits.
                                            {key_field, key_type}
                                              Key on ONE field: `Map<{key_type}, List<Imp>>`
                                              keyed on `extImp.get<Field>()`. Upstream uses
                                              this with String (ThirtyThreeAcrossBidder),
                                              Integer (AdtargetBidder) and an enum
                                              (TaboolaBidder), so key_type is REQUIRED here
                                              rather than assumed to be String — the previous
                                              revision hardcoded String and therefore could
                                              not express adkernel, whose key is an Integer
                                              zoneId. key_field must be a lower-camelCase Java
                                              identifier; the SKILL owns any snake_case
                                              normalization (Rule 46) before it lands here.
                                          `HashMap`, not `LinkedHashMap`: all six merged Java
                                          groupers use HashMap, and Go's own fixture harness
                                          matches requests order-insensitively on purpose
                                          (`adapters/adapterstest/test_json.go`: "try to match
                                          expected to actual without assuming order, as the use
                                          of maps in some adapters purposely randomizes
                                          order"). If a bidder genuinely needs a stable
                                          outgoing order, that is a per-bidder decision to make
                                          explicitly, not a default to inherit.
  ctx.endpoint_resolution_kind : str  — one of {"static", "single-token-substitution",
                                          "query-parameter-augmentation", "dev-prod-toggle",
                                          "multi-token-substitution"}; Rule 11/12/13/14
  ctx.headers_collapse         : bool — Rule 19; emit HttpUtil.headers() shorthand
  ctx.http_status_kind         : str  — one of {"canonical-helpers", "legacy-raw"}; Rule 30
  ctx.bid_type_resolution      : str  — one of {"imp-mediatype-introspection",
                                          "ext-prebid-video-placement",
                                          "constant-banner",
                                          "by-bid-mtype",
                                          "method-chain-fallback"}; Rule 23-25
  ctx.bid_type_error_tolerance : str  — one of {"abort-all" (default), "per-bid-skip"}.
                                          Only meaningful with
                                          bid_type_resolution == "by-bid-mtype"; any other
                                          pairing fails at render. "abort-all" throws
                                          PreBidException on an unresolved mtype, which
                                          discards the whole makeBids result;
                                          "per-bid-skip" accumulates a badServerResponse
                                          error and SKIPS that bid while its siblings
                                          continue. Read this off the SOURCE bid loop, not
                                          off taste: Go `errs = append(errs, err); continue`
                                          inside the seatbid walk is per-bid-skip, a Go
                                          `return nil, err` is abort-all. Target-repo shape
                                          for per-bid-skip: ZentotemBidder (68 upstream
                                          adapters take an errors list into extractBids).
  ctx.multiformat_supported    : bool — mirrors bidder-config meta-info
                                          {app,site,dooh}-media-types declaring
                                          >1 media type. When true, resolveBidType
                                          MUST use bid_type_resolution=="by-bid-mtype"
                                          (imp introspection is fallback only); an
                                          imp-only resolution fails loudly at render
                                          — a multiformat imp carries co-present
                                          formats imp priority cannot disambiguate
                                          (Teal #4765). Defaults false when omitted.
  ctx.javadoc_summary          : str|null  — class-level Javadoc
  ctx.imports_extra            : list[str]  — caller-collected; alphabetically sorted

The body shape per kobler is:
  - private final {endpoint, currencyConversionService, mapper}
  - public ctor(endpoint, [currencyConversionService,] mapper) { ... HttpUtil.validateUrl ... }
  - makeHttpRequests: parse imp.ext per imp, build HttpRequest, return
  - makeBids: parse BidResponse, walk seatbid → bid, classify type, return
  - private helpers: parseImpExt, getBidType

Variants beyond canonical surface as unresolved_translations[] entries
when the SKILL's Step 3 cannot deterministically map a rule to template
inputs.
#}
